@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:apps_lxd.component.confirmation_checkbox a ds:Component;
    ds:name "ConfirmationCheckbox";
    ds:summary "The **ConfirmationCheckbox** extends the ConfirmationModal with a checkbox in the footer of the modal. It is used where users must explicitly acknowledge or confirm specific conditions before proceeding with an action. The action is usually dangerous and/or permanent.\n\n\n\n**Main use cases**:\n\n1. **Force action confirmation** - the below actions can be perform with or without `force` flag:\n\n  - Force stopping running instances\n  - Force deleting active instances\n  - Force restarting instances in problematic states\n\n1. **Prerequisite acknowledgment** - Ensures users have completed required steps before continuing:\n\n  - users confirm they have copied authentication token in a safe place after creating an identity (in this case, the `Done` button is disabled until the **ConfirmationCheckbox** is checked)\n  - users confirm they acknowledge data loss warnings in destructive operations (eg restoring an instance “with state” when using a snapshot of the instance)\n  - users confirm they understand irreversible actions (eg permanently deleting an entity)\n\n\n\n**When to use**:\n\n- ✅ When you need an additional safety check before executing potentially harmful actions\n- ✅ When users must acknowledge they understand the consequences of their action\n- ✅ When implementing `force` variants of standard operations\n- ✅ When users need to confirm completion of prerequisite steps\n- ✅ In confirmation modals where state-controlled checkbox behavior is needed";
    ds:anatomyDsl "---\nnode:\n    uri: lxd.component.ConfirmationCheckbox\n    styles:\n      layout.type: flow\n      layout.direction: horizontal\n      layout.align: start\n      layout.float: left\n    edges:\n      - node:\n          role: wrapper container\n          styles:\n            layout.display: inline\n            layout.float: left\n          edges:\n            - node:\n                uri: canonical:component:CheckboxInput\n                styles:\n                  layout.display: inline\n                  interaction.tabindex: -1\n                  form.type: checkbox\n                  form.controlled: true\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1..1\"\n                slotName: default\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"1..1\"";
    ds:anatomyClassic "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n";
    ds:usage "## **General description**\n\nThe **ConfirmationCheckbox** extends the ConfirmationModal with a checkbox in the footer of the modal. It is used where users must explicitly acknowledge or confirm specific conditions before proceeding with an action. The action is usually dangerous and/or permanent.\n\n\n\n## Implementation guidelines\n\n### When to use\n\n Use the **ConfirmationCheckbox** when you need to ensure users explicitly acknowledge risks, consequences, or prerequisites before allowing them to proceed. This component serves as a safety gate in critical workflows where user understanding and intention must be verified.\n\n**When to use**:\n\n- ✅ When you need an additional safety check before executing potentially harmful actions\n- ✅ When users must acknowledge they understand the consequences of their action\n- ✅ When implementing `force` variants of standard operations\n- ✅ When users need to confirm completion of prerequisite steps\n- ✅ In confirmation modals where state-controlled checkbox behavior is needed\n\n\n\n**When not to use**:\n\n- ❌ For simple boolean preferences, settings or standard form inputs: in scenarios where you need basic checkbox functionality, use the standard CheckboxInput component instead.\n- ❌ For low-risk operation: avoid using this component for actions that can be easily undone or have minimal consequences, as it would create unnecessary friction.\n- ❌ When accessibility requirements demand standard keyboard navigation: the component sets `tabIndex={-1}` which removes it from the tab order, making it unsuitable for forms that must support full keyboard accessibility.\n\n\n\n## Implementation notes\n\nThe component requires a React state tuple `[boolean, Dispatch<SetStateAction<boolean>>]` passed as the `confirmed` prop. This controlled pattern ensures the confirmation state is managed by the parent component and can be used to control the availability of subsequent actions.";
    ds:guidelines "### Accessibility\n\n**Non-standard focus behavior:** This component deliberately uses `tabIndex={-1}` to remove the checkbox from standard keyboard navigation flow. This design choice acknowledges that confirmation checkboxes are secondary actions that should be activated through mouse interaction or alternative keyboard shortcuts within their containing modal or dialog.\n\n**Screen reader compatibility**: The underlying CheckboxInput component maintains proper ARIA attributes and semantic markup. Screen readers will correctly announce the checkbox label and state.\n\n### Content specification\n\n- **Concise:** Keep the label concise, as it has to fit in the footer of the ConfirmationModal, usually next to action buttons.";
    ds:tier ds:apps_lxd;
    ds:hasProperty [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "label";
        ds:summary "Text displays next to the checbox";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:optional "false"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "confirmed";
        ds:summary "React useState const [isConfirmed, setConfirmed] = confirmed;";
        ds:propertyType "[boolean, Dispatch<SetStateAction<boolean>>]";
        ds:optional "false"
    ].
